      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's true that you are a constant reminder of their sacrifice, and that weight is immense, but you are also the living proof of their love, even if you can't see it right now. The idea that you are a failure is a narrative you've built around yourself, and it's a very heavy one to carry. Think about how much effort it takes just to keep going when you feel this broken; that effort itself is something. Maybe the only way to stop reminding them of what they gave up is to finally give yourself the grace to just *be* without the pressure to be perfect.",
