      "content": "but being \"imperfect\" doesn't fix the damage. i see the way they look at me, like they're trying to find the person they expected me to be, but they only find this disappointment. it feels like the only way to actually protect them from that disappointment is to just stop being a part of it. if i could just disappear, the dream they had would stay intact instead of being ruined by the reality of me. it feels like the most selfless thing i could even do is just not be a burden anymore.",
